"Paul E Collins" <find_my_real_address@CL4.org> writes:
> Some of the monsters in NetHack are pretty resourceful, as I
> discovered when an otherwise harmless gnome managed to kill me by
> hurling a (pbpxngevpr rtt). I've also seen monsters gain an advantage
> by reading and quaffing certain scrolls and potions.
> 
> So, how exactly do monsters know what they are carrying? Can they
> identify things?

No. They usually don't need to; the game will generally let a monster
know (or rather, let it make decisions based on a knowledge of):

* what type of object something is
* how many charges, or what enchantment, it has

but _not_:

* whether it's blessed, uncursed, or cursed

These assumptions are explicitly arbitrary, though the choices seem
motivated mainly by a combination of balance considerations and a
desire not to have to keep minute track of what each monster knows
about each object.

